WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.769 --> 00:00:06.911
Thanks for making time
for your momma bear.

2
00:00:06.936 --> 00:00:09.399
Well. you know we said we was
gonna do this thing monthly.

3
00:00:09.424 --> 00:00:11.801
Besides. it's spring break.

4
00:00:11.826 --> 00:00:13.650
and my life ain't
crazy for once.

5
00:00:15.019 --> 00:00:17.582
This is feeling like old times.

6
00:00:19.844 --> 00:00:22.087
Hot cakes fresh off the skillet.

7
00:00:22.112 --> 00:00:23.653
Hey.

8
00:00:23.828 --> 00:00:25.490
Did I show you to mix water

9
00:00:25.515 --> 00:00:27.052
instead of milk
with that batter?

10
00:00:27.077 --> 00:00:29.174
Yes. ma'am. Less
calories and fat.

11
00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:30.797
And Spencer loves
them. Right. baby?

12
00:00:30.822 --> 00:00:31.748
Yeah.

13
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:36.941
You want some. Mrs. Grace?

14
00:00:36.966 --> 00:00:40.420
You know. I am going to
stick with these biscuits.

15
00:00:40.445 --> 00:00:41.445
Ok.

16
00:00:47.198 --> 00:00:48.341
Hey. girl.

17
00:00:48.366 --> 00:00:50.588
Denise. You're early.

18
00:00:50.613 --> 00:00:52.615
Early for what?
- Uh...

19
00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:58.223
There's something that I've
been wanting to show you.

20
00:01:03.388 --> 00:01:05.004
Where the hell is my bed?

21
00:01:05.029 --> 00:01:07.452
You know how I always said
I wanted a craft room?

22
00:01:07.477 --> 00:01:09.769
Well. Denise inspired
me to get started.

23
00:01:09.794 --> 00:01:11.496
I love this idea.

24
00:01:11.562 --> 00:01:13.413
You know. we have tons of fabric

25
00:01:13.438 --> 00:01:14.894
at the dress shop
that you can have.

26
00:01:14.919 --> 00:01:16.581
Oh. girl. bring it on over!

27
00:01:16.606 --> 00:01:18.868
She is officially hired to
help. I like her. Come on.

28
00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:19.952
Wait. Wait. Wait. Wait. Wait.

29
00:01:19.976 --> 00:01:21.678
Where am I supposed to
sleep when I come home?

30
00:01:21.702 --> 00:01:23.163
Your home is at the beach house.

31
00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:25.306
where you've been
living for the past year

32
00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:26.781
with your comfortable bed.

33
00:01:26.806 --> 00:01:27.964
You know. when you're here.

34
00:01:27.989 --> 00:01:29.691
you can always sleep on
the blow up mattress.

35
00:01:29.715 --> 00:01:31.236
This wall is larger
than I thought.

36
00:01:31.261 --> 00:01:32.672
We could put a kiln over here!

37
00:01:32.697 --> 00:01:33.636
What the hell is a kiln?

38
00:01:33.661 --> 00:01:35.162
We're not putting
a kiln in here.

39
00:01:35.187 --> 00:01:36.848
I made this necklace in a kiln.

40
00:01:36.873 --> 00:01:39.132
- Oh. That is nice.
- Ok. I'm out.

41
00:01:39.157 --> 00:01:39.925
Wait. Spencer.

42
00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:42.333
Nope. S'all good. I got
morning practice anyways.

43
00:01:42.358 --> 00:01:45.370
so y'all can just do whatever.

44
00:01:45.395 --> 00:01:47.397
Uh...

45
00:01:52.071 --> 00:01:55.295
Are you sure you don't
wanna stay a little longer?

46
00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.502
I could have coffee
and donuts delivered.

47
00:01:57.527 --> 00:01:59.709
I wish. My schedule
is so jammed.

48
00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:01.946
I literally had to set
reminders to take my vitamins.

49
00:02:01.971 --> 00:02:05.265
How 'bout. hey. dinner and a
movie in the Marina tomorrow?

50
00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:08.508
Nope. Back to back
meetings and vitamins.

51
00:02:08.533 --> 00:02:12.677
Ok. You're still coming to Liv's award
ceremony. tonight. though. right?

52
00:02:12.777 --> 00:02:14.755
I feel terrible. but there's
an artist in town from the UK

53
00:02:14.779 --> 00:02:16.241
I have to scope out.

54
00:02:16.341 --> 00:02:17.602
And I already spoke to Liv.

55
00:02:17.627 --> 00:02:18.923
She said she's cool.

56
00:02:18.948 --> 00:02:20.447
I'm just gonna get
her flowers. though.

57
00:02:20.471 --> 00:02:22.567
But cheer loudly
for the both of us?

58
00:02:22.592 --> 00:02:25.615
Sure. Bye.

59
00:02:27.171 --> 00:02:28.592
Studying?

60
00:02:28.617 --> 00:02:30.879
No. It's spring break.

61
00:02:31.008 --> 00:02:34.312
Well. then why don't you take
a break like everybody else?

62
00:02:34.337 --> 00:02:36.417
Well. I'm writing a speech
for the award ceremony.

63
00:02:36.441 --> 00:02:38.343
I mean. I know winning
is a long shot.

64
00:02:38.368 --> 00:02:41.140
But if I do. then everyone's
gonna be asking for my next story.

65
00:02:41.165 --> 00:02:43.447
Actually. would you mind
listening to what I've got so far?

66
00:02:43.471 --> 00:02:45.453
Sure! I'm all ears.

67
00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:47.832
Um...

68
00:02:48.007 --> 00:02:50.750
Do you need help
finding something?

69
00:02:50.775 --> 00:02:53.638
No. just organising versions
one through four of my speech.

70
00:02:53.663 --> 00:02:55.405
You're going to read
me four versions?

71
00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:57.532
Seven. The last three
are on my computer.

72
00:03:05.665 --> 00:03:07.166
Hey. Hi.

73
00:03:07.191 --> 00:03:09.048
What's up with the 911 text?

74
00:03:09.073 --> 00:03:12.577
I think Liv is spiralling with
this whole award ceremony.

75
00:03:12.677 --> 00:03:14.455
Well. I mean. I'm sure there's
a lot of pressure. Right?

76
00:03:14.479 --> 00:03:16.381
I mean. this is a
huge deal for her.

77
00:03:16.406 --> 00:03:18.017
Maybe just give her some space?

78
00:03:18.042 --> 00:03:19.784
Well. she asked for my help.

79
00:03:19.809 --> 00:03:21.364
And then she kicked
me out of her room

80
00:03:21.389 --> 00:03:23.845
after my third
note on draft two.

81
00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:24.905
How many drafts are there?

82
00:03:24.929 --> 00:03:26.325
Don't ask.

83
00:03:29.414 --> 00:03:31.516
You know what?

84
00:03:31.691 --> 00:03:34.073
The last time that
she spoke publicly.

85
00:03:34.098 --> 00:03:35.880
it didn't go so well.

86
00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:38.163
Maybe she just doesn't want
a repeat of the eulogy.

87
00:03:38.188 --> 00:03:39.919
Yeah. I'll go check on her.

88
00:03:39.944 --> 00:03:41.366
Thank you.

89
00:03:43.703 --> 00:03:46.005
You're not worried your
fingers might fall off?

90
00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:48.012
That's the least of my concerns.

91
00:03:48.037 --> 00:03:50.415
Yeah. you got half the
Amazon forest on your floor.

92
00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:51.875
Yeah. well. who
needs trees. right?

93
00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:53.756
- Whoa.
- I'm kidding.

94
00:03:53.781 --> 00:03:55.992
Well. at least you're still
cracking jokes. That's a good sign.

95
00:03:56.016 --> 00:03:59.340
Jordan. what if people think I'm a fraud
when they realise I'm not Jayden Davis?

96
00:03:59.364 --> 00:04:01.706
Ok. Maybe it's time we. uh.
step away from the keyboard.

97
00:04:01.731 --> 00:04:02.789
No. I'm in a groove.

98
00:04:02.814 --> 00:04:04.816
Draft eight is
feeling really solid.

99
00:04:06.638 --> 00:04:08.019
Draft eight. you say?

100
00:04:08.044 --> 00:04:09.694
Yeah. Wow. That's cool.

101
00:04:09.719 --> 00:04:12.183
What are you doing? I was just
in the middle of a clever segue.

102
00:04:12.207 --> 00:04:14.515
Yeah. You got two hours to work on
that segue while I'm at practice.

103
00:04:14.539 --> 00:04:16.000
and then you're
going away with me.

104
00:04:16.025 --> 00:04:17.073
What part of "i
need to work..."?

105
00:04:17.097 --> 00:04:20.280
Non-negotiable. Olivia baker.

106
00:04:20.605 --> 00:04:22.307
Two.

107
00:04:25.934 --> 00:04:27.372
♪ Yeah. who dat... ♪

108
00:04:27.397 --> 00:04:28.699
Here we go. Down. Set.

109
00:04:28.724 --> 00:04:29.760
Watch out. Watch out.

110
00:04:29.784 --> 00:04:31.211
Wide 16. Here we
go. Here we go.

111
00:04:31.235 --> 00:04:33.281
Hey. check 5. check 5. check 5.

112
00:04:33.385 --> 00:04:34.787
Wide 16.

113
00:04:34.812 --> 00:04:36.100
Set.

114
00:04:36.387 --> 00:04:38.209
♪ ...so don't be
jealous with it ♪

115
00:04:38.363 --> 00:04:39.784
♪ watch me get it. yeah ♪

116
00:04:39.884 --> 00:04:41.866
♪ inside. outside. yeah ♪

117
00:04:41.966 --> 00:04:43.348
Uh!

118
00:04:43.373 --> 00:04:45.019
We need fast feet. boys!

119
00:04:46.651 --> 00:04:48.063
Boy. where'd you get
that whistle from?

120
00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:49.331
Found it. Yeah?

121
00:04:49.356 --> 00:04:50.777
Come meet the team. Come on.

122
00:04:50.802 --> 00:04:52.592
You let sal catch up
to you. didn't you?

123
00:04:52.617 --> 00:04:53.930
Boost his confidence?

124
00:04:53.955 --> 00:04:56.818
Nah. Just ain't got it today.

125
00:04:57.140 --> 00:05:00.764
Hey. did they change your
bedroom when you moved out?

126
00:05:00.905 --> 00:05:02.967
Coop lives in my old room.

127
00:05:03.067 --> 00:05:04.609
That don't bother you?

128
00:05:04.709 --> 00:05:06.971
Nope. It still
feels like home.

129
00:05:07.968 --> 00:05:08.949
Hey. is that. uh...?

130
00:05:08.974 --> 00:05:10.209
Dr. Gutenberg.

131
00:05:10.234 --> 00:05:12.337
- Gau's president.
- Yeah.

132
00:05:12.362 --> 00:05:14.014
Man. I ain't seen him
since the day I signed.

133
00:05:14.038 --> 00:05:15.193
What the hell's he doing here?

134
00:05:15.217 --> 00:05:16.373
Maybe he's looking for coach?

135
00:05:16.397 --> 00:05:18.399
- I'll go find out.
- Yeah.

136
00:05:22.407 --> 00:05:25.430
Dr. Gutenberg. I didn't
know you was a football fan.

137
00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:27.872
I'm not. but I am a booster fan.

138
00:05:27.897 --> 00:05:30.466
And there's a rumour our team is
signing ex-cons and has-been players.

139
00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:32.752
Where's coach
Kenny? Or any coach?

140
00:05:32.777 --> 00:05:35.194
We running student-led voluntary
practices for spring break.

141
00:05:35.219 --> 00:05:37.001
Coach Kenny is out in
Tennessee recruiting.

142
00:05:37.026 --> 00:05:38.026
So are the rumours true?

143
00:05:38.051 --> 00:05:40.674
No. I mean yes. yes.

144
00:05:40.699 --> 00:05:42.602
We have a guy who
made a mistake.

145
00:05:42.627 --> 00:05:44.765
but he did his time and now
he's getting a second chance.

146
00:05:44.789 --> 00:05:47.814
Golden Angeles university
is a prestigious program.

147
00:05:48.406 --> 00:05:49.771
It's not a charity case.

148
00:05:49.796 --> 00:05:51.210
This ain't charity. sir.

149
00:05:51.235 --> 00:05:53.573
All I know is my
elite d1 program that

150
00:05:53.598 --> 00:05:55.490
normally signs the top
players in the country

151
00:05:55.515 --> 00:05:56.831
now looks like last chance u.

152
00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:59.441
And the boosters aren't happy.
which means I'm not happy.

153
00:05:59.466 --> 00:06:01.207
They have a lot of questions.

154
00:06:01.232 --> 00:06:02.290
And if they don't
like the answers.

155
00:06:02.314 --> 00:06:04.716
I'll have no choice but
to clean house myself.

156
00:06:17.134 --> 00:06:19.003
What did he mean
by "clean house"?

157
00:06:19.103 --> 00:06:20.685
Is he gonna pull scholarships?

158
00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:24.254
Yeah. I'm not sure.
He ain't seem happy.

159
00:06:24.429 --> 00:06:27.051
I left a message with coach
Kenny to give him a heads up.

160
00:06:27.151 --> 00:06:28.292
I hope he got a plan.

161
00:06:28.317 --> 00:06:30.375
Wow! Look at you.

162
00:06:30.475 --> 00:06:32.527
Spencer James not
saving the world.

163
00:06:33.825 --> 00:06:36.611
Dr. Spears said I gotta chill
on all that. so I'm trying.

164
00:06:36.636 --> 00:06:38.257
I see you. I see you.

165
00:06:38.282 --> 00:06:40.299
But. look. I gotta run
somewhere with Liv.

166
00:06:40.324 --> 00:06:42.987
But. uh. you're still coming to
her award ceremony tonight. right?

167
00:06:43.012 --> 00:06:44.427
Oh. my bad.

168
00:06:44.452 --> 00:06:46.467
I thought that was just a
family invite-only thing.

169
00:06:46.491 --> 00:06:48.753
And I got this date with Alicia.

170
00:06:48.853 --> 00:06:51.516
I don't know how cool she'd be
if I rescheduled that for Liv.

171
00:06:51.541 --> 00:06:53.242
Yeah. don't do that.

172
00:06:53.267 --> 00:06:54.737
It's all good.
I'll see you later.

173
00:06:54.779 --> 00:06:56.781
All right. man.

174
00:06:57.582 --> 00:06:59.159
- That-a boy.
- What's up. man?

175
00:06:59.183 --> 00:07:01.285
How you feeling
about everything?

176
00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:03.390
So who was that grumpy-looking
white dude you was talking to?

177
00:07:03.414 --> 00:07:04.844
That was gau's president.

178
00:07:04.869 --> 00:07:06.214
The big man. huh?
- Mm-hmm.

179
00:07:06.238 --> 00:07:08.752
I'm guessing he's wondering where
his usual five-star recruits are.

180
00:07:08.753 --> 00:07:10.970
Hey. Don't trip. He
don't get football.

181
00:07:10.995 --> 00:07:12.282
S'all good.

182
00:07:12.307 --> 00:07:14.966
It ain't like five-star recruits
have it easy these days anyway.

183
00:07:15.459 --> 00:07:17.216
I been training Marco galvez.

184
00:07:17.241 --> 00:07:18.623
Oh. I know Marco.

185
00:07:18.723 --> 00:07:20.144
Yeah. He was about
to sign with us

186
00:07:20.169 --> 00:07:21.621
before everything went down.

187
00:07:21.646 --> 00:07:22.987
I thought he went to Florida.

188
00:07:23.012 --> 00:07:24.864
Well. he's in town
on spring break.

189
00:07:24.889 --> 00:07:26.849
Sound like he not having
the best time down there.

190
00:07:26.884 --> 00:07:28.868
Why? What's up?
- I didn't ask.

191
00:07:28.893 --> 00:07:30.871
I'm training him here in
an hour if you wanna join.

192
00:07:30.895 --> 00:07:32.997
Might be nice for him
to see a familiar face.

193
00:07:33.022 --> 00:07:34.891
For sure. I'm gonna definitely
swing by. Good looking out.

194
00:07:34.915 --> 00:07:35.915
Of course.

195
00:07:37.115 --> 00:07:38.037
Ok.

196
00:07:38.062 --> 00:07:39.924
so the interview should
be pretty seamless.

197
00:07:39.949 --> 00:07:41.360
He's just gonna
be. like. fishing

198
00:07:41.385 --> 00:07:43.463
for what fans can expect
from the "fire & ice" tour.

199
00:07:43.488 --> 00:07:46.634
So. yeah. just keep it.
like. vague. but exciting.

200
00:07:46.659 --> 00:07:48.888
Cool.

201
00:07:48.913 --> 00:07:50.054
Cool. cool.

202
00:07:50.079 --> 00:07:52.021
Uh. yeah. so that
right there was

203
00:07:52.046 --> 00:07:54.108
the opposite of exciting.

204
00:07:54.133 --> 00:07:57.021
Well. I was actually thinkin'
about that quinceañera.

205
00:07:57.074 --> 00:07:58.532
That was so fun. wasn't it?

206
00:07:58.557 --> 00:07:59.739
Yeah.

207
00:07:59.764 --> 00:08:01.546
Um. remember how I told you

208
00:08:01.571 --> 00:08:03.503
it reminded me about

209
00:08:03.528 --> 00:08:05.750
how much I miss my
indie boho roots?

210
00:08:05.776 --> 00:08:06.899
Mm-hmm.

211
00:08:06.924 --> 00:08:08.719
Yeah. Well. I
kinda... I don't know.

212
00:08:08.746 --> 00:08:10.950
Patience. whatever
it is. just say it.

213
00:08:10.975 --> 00:08:12.620
I just. I mean. we
poured so much time

214
00:08:12.645 --> 00:08:15.852
and resources into this
new image and sound...

215
00:08:15.877 --> 00:08:16.972
But you know what?

216
00:08:16.997 --> 00:08:19.706
Talking out loud is the
confirmation that I need.

217
00:08:19.731 --> 00:08:21.392
So. yeah. let's just...

218
00:08:21.417 --> 00:08:22.683
Let's just keep
this train moving.

219
00:08:22.707 --> 00:08:24.484
- Are you sure?
- Yes. I am sure.

220
00:08:24.508 --> 00:08:25.456
Look. we got this interview.

221
00:08:25.481 --> 00:08:27.543
and it's gonna be dope. Yeah.

222
00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:31.261
But you know what
I'm not sure about

223
00:08:31.286 --> 00:08:33.028
is your phone stressing
with them alerts.

224
00:08:33.053 --> 00:08:34.487
Sorry. it's my calendar.

225
00:08:34.512 --> 00:08:36.656
There's. like. a million
things to do and no time.

226
00:08:36.681 --> 00:08:39.824
Including this brunch with
my dad which I need to cancel

227
00:08:39.849 --> 00:08:42.472
'cause your interviewer
changed the interview time.

228
00:08:42.533 --> 00:08:45.184
Oh. no. no. no. Just go be
with your dad. I got this.

229
00:08:45.209 --> 00:08:47.347
- No. I should be here.
- Skye's gonna be there.

230
00:08:47.371 --> 00:08:49.193
Look. why do you
have a hired staff

231
00:08:49.218 --> 00:08:51.230
if you don't trust
them to do their jobs?

232
00:08:51.255 --> 00:08:53.588
Ok. Thank you.

233
00:08:57.989 --> 00:08:59.727
What's this?

234
00:08:59.752 --> 00:09:01.213
Ha ha ha! A dance studio.

235
00:09:01.278 --> 00:09:02.700
I can see that. Jordan.

236
00:09:02.725 --> 00:09:05.169
How hard is the
nostalgia hitting?

237
00:09:06.997 --> 00:09:10.581
I mean. my last
memory here was. um.

238
00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:12.812
throwing a tutu in
Gina price's face.

239
00:09:12.837 --> 00:09:15.299
Mm-hmm. Dance was your
first language. right?

240
00:09:15.332 --> 00:09:16.914
It was how you
expressed yourself

241
00:09:16.939 --> 00:09:18.678
before you could even talk.

242
00:09:18.703 --> 00:09:22.073
So. I figured... why not
bring you back to your roots?

243
00:09:22.098 --> 00:09:24.120
How is this supposed
to help with my speech?

244
00:09:24.145 --> 00:09:26.848
Ok. You know better
than anyone that

245
00:09:26.873 --> 00:09:29.749
whenever I am feeling stuck
with football or life.

246
00:09:29.774 --> 00:09:31.281
I escape to video games.

247
00:09:31.306 --> 00:09:33.833
Now. some people
may call that lazy.

248
00:09:33.858 --> 00:09:35.760
but it's the outlet that I need.

249
00:09:35.785 --> 00:09:37.487
So maybe this can be
that for you again.

250
