00:28:43.232 --> 00:28:44.894
So...

758
00:28:44.919 --> 00:28:46.701
♪ I can do anything ♪

759
00:28:46.726 --> 00:28:48.468
♪ everything. all that ♪

760
00:28:48.493 --> 00:28:50.253
♪ say I ain't the baddest.
but we both know ♪

761
00:28:50.286 --> 00:28:52.542
♪ that's all cap.
see. we heating up ♪

762
00:28:52.567 --> 00:28:54.597
♪ our position.
better fall back ♪

763
00:28:54.622 --> 00:28:55.884
♪ you don't want no smoke ♪

764
00:28:55.909 --> 00:28:58.091
♪ getting faded
off the contact ♪

765
00:28:58.116 --> 00:29:00.218
♪ yeah. I bring the
fire every day ♪

766
00:29:00.243 --> 00:29:01.927
♪ ice cold at night ♪

767
00:29:01.952 --> 00:29:03.654
♪ got me switching up a Lane ♪

768
00:29:03.679 --> 00:29:06.423
♪ I can toe that line ♪

769
00:29:07.017 --> 00:29:09.840
It's really good.
It's better than good.

770
00:29:09.865 --> 00:29:12.928
Yeah? Ok. and I know... I
know reimagining the tour

771
00:29:12.981 --> 00:29:15.618
will unravel
everything. but I...

772
00:29:15.643 --> 00:29:17.300
I am down to work overtime.

773
00:29:17.325 --> 00:29:20.228
It's triple overtime for
me. But whatever it takes.

774
00:29:20.253 --> 00:29:22.395
And. yeah. and if it's
too much. I get it.

775
00:29:22.420 --> 00:29:25.063
Stop. Look. I don't care how
much work it's gonna take.

776
00:29:25.088 --> 00:29:27.070
This is the real Patience.

777
00:29:27.095 --> 00:29:29.918
And honestly. between the
quinceañera and today.

778
00:29:29.943 --> 00:29:32.290
this is. like. the happiest
I've heard you sound.

779
00:29:32.315 --> 00:29:33.352
Your fans are going to love it.

780
00:29:33.376 --> 00:29:34.618
- Seriously?
- Yeah.

781
00:29:34.642 --> 00:29:38.321
Cool. Um. ok. so we're
really doing this?

782
00:29:38.346 --> 00:29:39.688
Yeah. I mean. Gia
is gonna flip.

783
00:29:39.713 --> 00:29:41.054
but we'll get her
onboard tomorrow.

784
00:29:41.078 --> 00:29:43.781
Ok. Thank you. Thank you.

785
00:29:44.060 --> 00:29:46.162
Oh. my god.

786
00:29:46.187 --> 00:29:47.651
Look. I just. I
want you to be you.

787
00:29:47.676 --> 00:29:49.127
So we're gonna figure it out.

788
00:29:49.152 --> 00:29:51.435
And I get to cancel tomorrow's
pyrotechnics meeting.

789
00:29:51.460 --> 00:29:53.442
so more free time for me.

790
00:29:53.467 --> 00:29:55.173
Gotta run. I'm
really proud of you.

791
00:29:55.198 --> 00:29:57.020
- Thank you.
- Bye.

792
00:29:57.120 --> 00:29:58.451
Yes! Girl!

793
00:29:58.476 --> 00:29:59.617
Yes.

794
00:30:06.609 --> 00:30:08.581
Don't act like you don't
want those samosas.

795
00:30:08.606 --> 00:30:10.508
Go for it.

796
00:30:10.533 --> 00:30:12.535
It's tempting.

797
00:30:13.643 --> 00:30:17.675
Um... I know
using Jayden Davis

798
00:30:17.700 --> 00:30:20.163
was supposed to
protect all of us

799
00:30:20.188 --> 00:30:22.235
and showing up here.
claiming the name.

800
00:30:22.260 --> 00:30:23.721
breaks that.

801
00:30:23.746 --> 00:30:26.169
I thought actually maybe that's

802
00:30:26.269 --> 00:30:27.730
why you weren't
gonna come tonight.

803
00:30:27.755 --> 00:30:29.692
I'm sorry I even
hesitated to come.

804
00:30:29.717 --> 00:30:31.452
It was just a misunderstanding.

805
00:30:31.477 --> 00:30:33.823
Listen. you showing up tonight.

806
00:30:33.876 --> 00:30:35.934
owning who you are.
that takes guts.

807
00:30:35.959 --> 00:30:38.456
And j. And I meant it when
we said we support you.

808
00:30:38.481 --> 00:30:41.945
And in terms of protection.
you know you got the vortex.

809
00:30:41.970 --> 00:30:45.073
Ain't nobody messing with us.

810
00:30:45.134 --> 00:30:47.797
Thanks. Spencer.

811
00:30:47.951 --> 00:30:49.933
How are your nerves
holding up. sweetie?

812
00:30:49.958 --> 00:30:52.020
Better-ish.

813
00:30:52.045 --> 00:30:53.787
Mm-hmm.

814
00:30:54.481 --> 00:30:56.314
Baby. uh.

815
00:30:56.339 --> 00:30:58.281
can I talk to you?

816
00:30:58.306 --> 00:30:59.845
Actually. I think
they're about to start.

817
00:30:59.869 --> 00:31:01.330
Maybe after the ceremony?

818
00:31:01.355 --> 00:31:04.018
Ok.

819
00:31:04.140 --> 00:31:06.923
Leaps of faith are scary.

820
00:31:07.150 --> 00:31:09.487
and bravery looks
different to everyone.

821
00:31:09.512 --> 00:31:12.250
To me. bravery looked
like the first time

822
00:31:12.275 --> 00:31:15.408
that I said out loud
I wanted to achieve

823
00:31:15.433 --> 00:31:17.535
what I thought was impossible.

824
00:31:17.560 --> 00:31:19.062
a career in the NBA.

825
00:31:19.087 --> 00:31:21.506
I guess my ancestors
were working overtime...

826
00:31:23.018 --> 00:31:25.623
Because four
championship rings later.

827
00:31:25.648 --> 00:31:29.031
I think I achieved
my dream. then some.

828
00:31:29.056 --> 00:31:31.714
And I continue to honour
those who came before me

829
00:31:31.739 --> 00:31:34.258
every day of my
life by living up

830
00:31:34.283 --> 00:31:36.287
to the best that they saw in me.

831
00:31:36.312 --> 00:31:38.239
And each nominee here tonight

832
00:31:38.264 --> 00:31:40.526
have their own story of bravery.

833
00:31:40.551 --> 00:31:43.374
leaps of faith on how
they changed lives.

834
00:31:43.399 --> 00:31:46.230
stories that will
thankfully live on

835
00:31:46.255 --> 00:31:48.366
in the articles that
they have written.

836
00:31:48.391 --> 00:31:52.095
So I am honored to present

837
00:31:52.120 --> 00:31:56.054
the award for excellence
in sports journalism.

838
00:31:56.079 --> 00:31:58.081
And it goes to...

839
00:32:00.043 --> 00:32:01.344
Jayden Davis.

840
00:32:03.378 --> 00:32:05.280
You won! You did it!

841
00:32:05.408 --> 00:32:06.870
Liv. you won.

842
00:32:06.970 --> 00:32:08.591
Except I can't move.

843
00:32:08.691 --> 00:32:10.553
I think I can help.

844
00:32:10.606 --> 00:32:12.608
Yeah.

845
00:32:16.139 --> 00:32:18.181
Thank you.

846
00:32:30.113 --> 00:32:31.808
Um...

847
00:32:40.118 --> 00:32:42.900
Um... hi.

848
00:32:42.925 --> 00:32:46.009
Thank you so much for this.

849
00:32:47.330 --> 00:32:49.467
In the spirit of Mr. Salley

850
00:32:49.492 --> 00:32:51.955
and those he continues to honor.

851
00:32:52.055 --> 00:32:54.347
I'd like to take this
moment to honor a man.

852
00:32:54.372 --> 00:32:58.036
without whom I'd never
have written this article.

853
00:32:58.061 --> 00:33:00.203
My dad passed away
a few months ago.

854
00:33:00.228 --> 00:33:02.832
I was supposed to honour him
with the eulogy at his funeral.

855
00:33:02.857 --> 00:33:08.486
but I couldn't find the air to
breathe. let alone the words.

856
00:33:08.511 --> 00:33:12.410
But if you'd indulge me. i'd
really like to try again today.

857
00:33:12.435 --> 00:33:16.059
My dad is Billy baker.

858
00:33:16.234 --> 00:33:18.030
Some of you may know him

859
00:33:18.055 --> 00:33:20.797
as former NFL great turned
high school football coach.

860
00:33:20.822 --> 00:33:25.007
but... he was so much more.

861
00:33:25.930 --> 00:33:30.033
He was a pillar of his
community in south L.A..

862
00:33:30.133 --> 00:33:34.797
a mentor to many. and
a friend to even more.

863
00:33:34.897 --> 00:33:39.021
a husband to the most
incredible and patient woman...

864
00:33:40.510 --> 00:33:43.613
And a father to all. even
if you weren't his blood.

865
00:33:43.652 --> 00:33:47.445
He encouraged me early on
in life to be a change maker

866
00:33:47.470 --> 00:33:51.124
and more recently.
to use journalism

867
00:33:51.149 --> 00:33:53.451
as my weapon against injustice.

868
00:33:53.476 --> 00:33:55.938
He also taught me to
be proud of my name

869
00:33:55.963 --> 00:33:57.429
and supported me

870
00:33:57.454 --> 00:34:00.048
even when I didn't feel
comfortable using it.

871
00:34:01.924 --> 00:34:03.987
So today.

872
00:34:04.087 --> 00:34:06.629
I'd like to reclaim that name

873
00:34:06.654 --> 00:34:08.676
as Olivia baker.

874
00:34:08.751 --> 00:34:10.873
not Jayden Davis.

875
00:34:13.456 --> 00:34:16.799
I'd like to dedicate
this award to my dad.

876
00:34:16.899 --> 00:34:19.362
a change maker himself

877
00:34:19.462 --> 00:34:22.945
and a man that we can
only aspire to be.

878
00:34:24.654 --> 00:34:26.776
I love you. dad.

879
00:34:28.271 --> 00:34:30.057
Thank you.

880
00:34:49.847 --> 00:34:52.430
Finally. she eats.

881
00:34:52.584 --> 00:34:54.432
The nerves are gone.

882
00:34:54.457 --> 00:34:56.599
Appetite's back.

883
00:34:57.073 --> 00:34:58.615
I'm proud of you. Liv.

884
00:34:58.640 --> 00:35:01.042
That was a beautiful tribute.

885
00:35:04.016 --> 00:35:05.902
Can I ask you something?

886
00:35:05.927 --> 00:35:07.669
Yeah. How do you do it?

887
00:35:07.694 --> 00:35:09.647
Put one foot in
front of the other

888
00:35:09.672 --> 00:35:12.890
after losing both
Corey and now my dad?

889
00:35:12.915 --> 00:35:15.498
I want to keep
honouring him every day.

890
00:35:15.523 --> 00:35:19.067
But I just... how?

891
00:35:19.092 --> 00:35:21.706
By learning to live in the now.

892
00:35:22.445 --> 00:35:25.748
That's what your pops
would have wanted for us.

893
00:35:26.001 --> 00:35:28.103
Liv. you and me.

894
00:35:28.130 --> 00:35:31.464
we had to learn the hard way
that we only got a small window.

895
00:35:31.489 --> 00:35:33.351
tomorrow ain't promised.

896
00:35:33.376 --> 00:35:35.378
So embrace what's
in front of you...

897
00:35:38.696 --> 00:35:40.352
Your dad would've wanted you

898
00:35:40.377 --> 00:35:42.919
to live out your wildest dreams

899
00:35:43.145 --> 00:35:45.776
both in your career
and your life.

900
00:35:45.801 --> 00:35:46.868
You're right.

901
00:35:46.893 --> 00:35:49.635
Can't say I've really
been doing that.

902
00:35:50.227 --> 00:35:52.770
I'm a freshman college student

903
00:35:52.795 --> 00:35:55.658
who's been so focused
on my job off campus.

904
00:35:55.758 --> 00:35:58.261
I don't even know where
the commissary is.

905
00:35:58.294 --> 00:35:59.286
Damn. Yeah.

906
00:35:59.311 --> 00:36:03.446
Ha ha! Well. look.
freshmen year ain't over.

907
00:36:05.147 --> 00:36:07.113
Go after the life you want.

908
00:36:15.914 --> 00:36:17.898
You gonna get it
changed to "Olivia"?

909
00:36:17.923 --> 00:36:19.677
I do wish it said
"Olivia baker."

910
00:36:19.702 --> 00:36:21.844
I'll get some sharpie on there.

911
00:36:21.869 --> 00:36:23.801
- This is so nice.
- So?

912
00:36:23.826 --> 00:36:25.828
- We're gonna be all right.
- Ha ha ha!

913
00:36:35.873 --> 00:36:37.735
I've been meaning to tell you

914
00:36:37.760 --> 00:36:38.976
that colour looks good on you.

915
00:36:39.001 --> 00:36:40.663
Oh. Thank you.

916
00:36:44.001 --> 00:36:46.744
There's something I've been
meaning to tell you. too.

917
00:36:46.769 --> 00:36:50.028
If it's about the craft
room. let me go first.

918
00:36:50.053 --> 00:36:53.311
I was selfish for trying to hold onto
something I should be letting go of.

919
00:36:53.336 --> 00:36:54.953
I shouldn't have
blindsided you like that.

920
00:36:54.977 --> 00:36:56.199
Yeah. well. it's your house.

921
00:36:56.224 --> 00:36:57.965
No. Spencer. it's our house.

922
00:36:57.990 --> 00:37:01.118
And in our house. you
sacrificed the world

923
00:37:01.143 --> 00:37:03.321
for me and Dillon to have
everything we needed.

924
00:37:03.346 --> 00:37:06.118
I should be honouring
that by honouring you

925
00:37:06.143 --> 00:37:07.920
and your needs now.

926
00:37:07.945 --> 00:37:11.008
Home ain't a place. ma.

927
00:37:11.108 --> 00:37:12.947
It's wherever you are.

928
00:37:12.972 --> 00:37:14.372
And all the craft
rooms in the world

929
00:37:14.397 --> 00:37:16.419
ain't gonna change that.

930
00:37:16.519 --> 00:37:18.521
You feel me?

931
00:37:20.082 --> 00:37:23.125
- Thank you. baby.
- Yep.

932
00:37:31.574 --> 00:37:33.588
Hey. Hi.

933
00:37:33.613 --> 00:37:35.353
Thought I would
find you in here.

934
00:37:35.378 --> 00:37:36.413
You working late?

935
00:37:36.438 --> 00:37:37.940
Uh. no. I was about
to join you guys.

936
00:37:37.965 --> 00:37:39.907
Just wanted to quickly
pack up some royalties

937
00:37:39.932 --> 00:37:42.159
so I don't forget to
mail them out tomorrow.

938
00:37:42.184 --> 00:37:45.688
Hmm. So what ever happened
with that UK artist?

939
00:37:45.713 --> 00:37:49.607
Oh. I sent the best a&r
consultant to cover for me.

940
00:37:49.632 --> 00:37:50.814
Really? You hired someone new?

941
00:37:50.838 --> 00:37:52.890
He wishes. It's my dad.

942
00:37:52.915 --> 00:37:55.368
But Liv's too important.

943
00:37:55.393 --> 00:37:57.094
I would've hated
to miss tonight.

944
00:37:57.119 --> 00:37:58.333
Hmm.

945
00:37:58.358 --> 00:38:02.104
And you're kind
of important. too.

946
00:38:02.129 --> 00:38:03.431
So. I was thinking...

947
00:38:03.456 --> 00:38:04.260
Mm-hmm.

948
00:38:04.285 --> 00:38:06.938
You've still got a few more
days left of spring break.

949
00:38:06.963 --> 00:38:10.013
so what do you think about
a day trip to Catalina?

950
00:38:10.038 --> 00:38:11.750
Well. I thought your
schedule was too tight.

951
00:38:11.774 --> 00:38:13.796
Now. where did this
sudden change come from?

952
00:38:13.821 --> 00:38:15.803
Time is fleeting.

953
00:38:15.978 --> 00:38:17.843
That's the tweet.

954
00:38:18.147 --> 00:38:19.369
Yeah.

955
00:38:19.415 --> 00:38:21.357
Yeah.

956
00:38:24.627 --> 00:38:26.689
Ok. Ooh. yup. yup.
That's the one.

957
00:38:26.722 --> 00:38:28.264
Yeah. That is the one.

958
00:38:28.289 --> 00:38:32.052
Ok. Post that with the
hashtag dream team.

959
00:38:33.382 --> 00:38:35.524
Cool. Um...

960
00:38:35.549 --> 00:38:37.420
You know. I wanted to thank you

961
00:38:37.445 --> 00:38:38.776
for your assist with Layla.

962
00:38:38.801 --> 00:38:41.117
Like. I owe you.

963
00:38:41.142 --> 00:38:42.625
It's your voice that sold it.

964
00:38:42.650 --> 00:38:44.942
You know. I feel
like. uh. my soul

965
00:38:44.967 --> 00:38:46.549
would've slowly died every day

966
00:38:46.574 --> 00:38:48.596
on the original tour. so...

967
00:38:48.621 --> 00:38:50.628
Well. now it can thrive
and inspire others

968
00:38:50.653 --> 00:38:51.834
the way it inspired me.

969
00:38:51.859 --> 00:38:52.667
Girl. quit it.

970
00:38:52.692 --> 00:38:53.982
No. I'm being for real.

971
00:38:54.007 --> 00:38:56.073
And watching you today
was the reminder I needed

972
00:38:56.098 --> 00:38:57.943
to always fight for me.

973
00:38:57.968 --> 00:38:59.642
I'm in awe of you. Patience.

974
00:38:59.667 --> 00:39:01.501
Wow.

975
00:39:01.526 --> 00:39:02.934
Well. thanks.

976
00:39:05.988 --> 00:39:07.405
Whoa. Um...

977
00:39:07.430 --> 00:39:08.811
Oh. my god.

978
00:39:08.911 --> 00:39:10.012
What the hell?

979
00:39:10.039 --> 00:39:11.374
Oh. I... I'm so sorry.

980
00:39:11.399 --> 00:39:12.225
I just... I got
carried away...

981
00:39:12.250 --> 00:39:14.093
No. Just... yeah. i'MMA go.

982
00:39:14.118 --> 00:39:17.262
Like. I... go.

983
00:39:17.600 --> 00:39:19.662
Yeah. I got to go.

984
00:39:19.748 --> 00:39:22.097
I... I got to...

985
00:39:40.708 --> 00:39:42.710
You wanted to see me. sir?

986
00:39:43.821 --> 00:39:45.843
I get the sense
you weren't happy

987
00:39:45.868 --> 00:39:48.372
with our talk earlier.

988
00:39:48.786 --> 00:39:51.809
No disrespect. but our team
doesn't need any fixing.

989
00:39:51.834 --> 00:39:53.497
Yeah. we got some guys
with some baggage.

990
00:39:53.522 --> 00:39:55.540
but they got something better
than any five-star recruit

991
00:39:55.564 --> 00:39:58.106
can offer... heart.

992
00:39:58.131 --> 00:39:59.862
So I keep being told.

993
00:39:59.887 --> 00:40:01.195
I don't understand. sir.

994
00:40:01.220 --> 00:40:02.275
You could have simply shared

995
00:40:02.299 --> 00:40:04.398
that the team had
re-signed Marco galvez

996
00:40:04.423 --> 00:40:05.550
instead of letting me believe

997
00:40:05.574 --> 00:40:07.527
it was just about these
second chance recruits.

998
00:40:07.552 --> 00:40:09.814
Well. first of all.
I'm not the coach.

999
00:40:10.011 --> 00:40:11.713
That would need to be
something coach Kenny

1000
00:40:11.738 --> 00:40:14.000
and a.D. Barnes would share
with you. if it was true.

1001
00:40:14.025 --> 00:40:15.407
Which it's not.

1002
00:40:15.432 --> 00:40:17.475
Actually it is.

1003
00:40:17.500 --> 00:40:19.642
Like I told
Dr. Gutenberg myself.

1004
00:40:19.667 --> 00:40:22.039
this roster is full
of heart. grit.

1005
00:40:22.064 --> 00:40:23.921
and dedication.

1006
00:40:23.946 --> 00:40:25.723
I'd regret not
being a part of it.

1007
00:40:25.748 --> 00:40:27.730
Wait. Are you coming to gau?

1008
00:40:27.755 --> 00:40:30.688
Y'all are rewriting your
narrative. just like me.

1009
00:40:30.713 --> 00:40:34.617
So. yes. I'm officially
decommitting from clearwater state

1010
00:40:34.642 --> 00:40:37.054
and joining gau.

1011
00:40:38.721 --> 00:40:41.063
The boosters had questions.

1012
00:40:41.088 --> 00:40:44.392
And now I get to deliver
some pretty great answers.

1013
00:40:44.567 --> 00:40:46.949
Looks like we got
ourselves a team.

